 "result_text": "I fixed it with a one-line change in `rachiopy/rachioobject.py`. I haven't run the tests or made a live API call, so the fix is untested.\n\n`_request` passed the request body to `requests` as `data=body`. With a dict, `requests` form-encodes it instead of sending JSON. The server then received something like `device=...` and rejected it with the \"Unrecognized token 'device'\" error. I changed it to `json=body`, so the body is now sent as real JSON.\n\nThe other payloads in `device.py`, `zone.py` and `schedulerule.py` are also dicts passed through the same function, so they get the same fix. `notification.add` and `notification.update` were just the calls where it showed up.\n\nAny test that asserts on the old `data=` argument will need updating. I didn't touch tests, as you asked.",
